The sprint board is built in `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/board-contract-haiku-3/app.contract` (view) and `app.ts` (data module), and all 26 visible tests pass after 8 of the 15 `./check`/`./test` runs. It uses one queued mutation per write with an echoed reply, so each `then` action can undo a declined change, and the data module returns read and write errors as data. I was unsure about: moves, adds and checklist writes being blocked while any column is in error (no hidden-test coverage for that); the rename field being cleared after a rename; and whether the server-side order of queued writes matches what the hidden tests expect.